# Blackheart frontend — systemd EnvironmentFile (OPTIONAL).
#
# Copy to /etc/blackheart/frontend.env, mode 600, root-owned:
#   sudo install -m 600 -o root -g root \
#     deploy/scripts/frontend.env.example /etc/blackheart/frontend.env
#
# IMPORTANT: NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are BAKED INTO THE BUILD on the CI runner
# (they end up in client-side JS and CSP headers — see next.config.mjs:13-30).
# Setting them here at runtime has no effect on what the browser sees. They
# belong in GitHub repo variables, NOT in this file:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL       (required for prod build — gh repo variable)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL        (required for prod build — gh repo variable)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_URL  (optional; collapses to API_URL when unset)
#
# This file is only for SERVER-side Next runtime knobs.

# Default runtime values are set on the systemd unit itself (NODE_ENV=production,
# PORT=3000, HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1). Override here only if you need to.

# Verbosity of the Next runtime. `info` is default; `debug` floods journald.
# NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1   # uncomment to disable Next telemetry
# NEXT_SHARP_PATH=/opt/blackheart-frontend/current/node_modules/sharp  # if image opt is added later
